`@db_cfg_arch ||= SharedFixtures.real_cfg_arch("_") rescue nil` rescues all `StandardError` and turns unexpected failures into silent skips. This can hide real regressions (e.g., if `real_cfg_arch` starts raising due to a bug). Prefer rescuing only the expected exception type(s) for “DB not available”, or check availability explicitly via a helper and let other exceptions fail the test.
```suggestion
    return @db_cfg_arch if defined?(@db_cfg_arch)

    begin
      @db_cfg_arch = SharedFixtures.real_cfg_arch("_")
    rescue RuntimeError
      # Real database (or fixtures) not available
      @db_cfg_arch = nil
    end
```
